WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.860
During its remarkably consistent and lengthy
run, It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia has

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:09.320
brought viewers the dark and hilarious adventures
of "the gang", who never learn the typical

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.920
sitcom lessons as they amusingly make the
world a worse place.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.940
It's an intimate, DIY affair, which makes
for a very loose set prone to improvisation.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.060
With that in mind, here are some of the funniest
bloopers ever captured during the filming

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.580
of It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:28.980
In season 10, the gang undertook one of its
most notorious activities to date: attempting

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.840
to match Hall of Famer Wade Boggs' supposed
off-the-field "record."

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.300
According to lore, Boggs once drank 70 beers
during a cross-country flight.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:42.700
Only Dee and Charlie make it all the way to
70 by the time their plane lands in Los Angeles,

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.300
but not without some consequences.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:49.020
It turns out that drinking that much beer
is going to make even the heaviest drinker

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.150
a little gassy.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.140
"That is disgusting."

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:51.660
"Give it to me.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:52.180
Two.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:52.680
Two.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.180
Two.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:53.680
Two."

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.140
"Oh my god!

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.240
It really is disgusting."

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.960
"It's pulled pork."

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.120
In this scene, two long-running plot threads
converge.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.670
The first: Dennis is most likely a psychopath,
and second: the gang is frequently dismissive

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:10.560
of Dee, the most reasonable person in their
midst.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.960
Dennis and Dee are twins, and yet nobody yells
at Dee with as much ferocity and venom as

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:16.460
Dennis.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.440
Here, he rants about as darkly as he's ever
ranted, so offended by some minor slight.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.220
"I will dice you into a tiny million little
pieces.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.240
I will shove you into a box."

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.080
"I will shove you into a box, and I'll put
that box into the freezer."

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:41.300
The Paddy's Pub crew has tried a lot of get-rich-quick
schemes, but none are as enduring as Fight

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:41.800
Milk.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:47.580
Charlie and Mac concocted this "alcoholic,
dairy-based protein drink for bodyguards by

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.100
bodyguards."

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.700
According to Charlie, it also, oddly, gives
consumers the strength of a crow.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.460
Mac and Charlie try to attract interest in
Fight Milk the way the gang usually promotes

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.220
a product: with a terrible, homemade commercial.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.240
These outtakes are from that ill-fated shoot.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.260
"What up?!

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:10.600
Do you have good ideas--"
"Fight milk!...Go, three, two, fight milk!"

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.260
In the seventh season, Mac puts on a large
amount of weight.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:21.909
Forever obsessed with physical fitness, he
proclaims that he's "cultivating mass," conflating

00:02:21.909 --> 00:02:24.740
adding flabby pounds to his body with getting
muscular.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:29.840
As a result, he spends a lot of his time eating
junk food, particularly in his down time,

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:33.120
like when he and Charlie are hanging out in
a van during a stakeout mission.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.540
Charlie just wants to snag one chip.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.980
"The world doesn't provide Charlie with chips
just because he wants chips, okay?

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:40.800
Don't care!

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:41.940
Don't ask again!"

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.960
One of Sunny's most popular recurring characters
is "Rickety Cricket," a former high school

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:53.709
classmate of the gang who went on to become
a priest, before hitting a downward spiral

00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:56.520
of homelessness, drug addiction, and disfigurement.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.260
This blooper comes from a scene in which Cricket
eats lemons for sustenance.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.659
Dennis has proven himself to a be a violent,
reckless person with a deep animosity for

00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:17.510
anything he perceives to be below his station
in life.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.599
In this fourth season clip, he and Charlie
walk into a pretty run-down home.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:27.280
Dennis immediately shows disdain by sarcastically
referring to the place as "charming" and "quaint."

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:31.640
Then, to emphasize his verbal eye-rolling,
he picks up a vase and throws it.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:34.260
"Whoa!

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.460
This isn't a breakable vase, dude."

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:38.760
"Is this a joke?"

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:44.639
Mac was raised almost entirely by his silent,
chain-smoking mother, as his father Luther

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.740
spent Mac's whole life in prison.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:51.519
Mac understandably has some daddy issues to
work through, and in a season two episode,

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:54.540
he tries to connect with Luther by visiting
him in the big house.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:59.840
When Mac offers to do whatever he can to win
his dad's love, he asks Mac and Charlie to

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.040
smuggle heroin into the prison for him.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:07.160
Mac tries to use the favor as a bargaining
chip, while Charlie gets a little over-enthusiastic.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.859
"But if you could just give us a little advice
on how to handle this situation, I promise

00:04:10.859 --> 00:04:12.280
we will come back our butts filled."

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:12.920
"Ugh!

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.160
Filled like a Christmas stocking."

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:21.540
Somehow, some way, Charlie gets a date in
one fifth season episode, so his friends provide

00:04:21.549 --> 00:04:23.410
lots of advice for the big night.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:27.629
For one, they specifically tell him to not
to eat any cheese, but Charlie can't help

00:04:27.629 --> 00:04:31.340
but eat cheese when he's nervous, and, well,
being on a date makes him nervous.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:35.820
Mac and Dennis find a workaround, telling
Charlie to just not breathe in the direction

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.860
of his companion, so instead he gives them
a whiff of his tremendously stinky cheese

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.360
breath.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:41.920
"Just don't breathe--ugh!"

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:42.420
"That's it.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:42.920
That's it.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.200
Wow."

